2. Meaningful reuse, notices and public attribution

"Meaningful Reuse" means distributing the whole project, a fork or port, or
copying or adapting an original implementation of a significant user-facing
feature from the Covered Material. It is determined by the functionality
transferred, not by a line count or a percentage of source code.

Isolated lines, small helper snippets, standard programming constructs and
API calls are excluded. Independently implementing a similar idea, writing
compatibility code, or interacting with the original project as a dependency
without incorporating its implementation is also excluded. These excluded
uses may be copied, modified and redistributed without reward sharing or
the additional public attribution requirement; retain applicable copyright
and license notices in copies or substantial portions as required below.

Include this license and the applicable copyright notices in all copies or
substantial portions of the Covered Material. When publicly distributing a
project involving Meaningful Reuse of the Covered Material, credit Antrakt92, identify ApplicantScout Companion as the source,
and provide a working link to the original project shown above in the project
description or accompanying documentation. Preserve these conditions for the
Covered Material in downstream copies; no endorsement by the author is implied.

3. CurseForge Reward Points

If that publicly distributed project earns CurseForge Reward Points, its
publisher must allocate at least 10% of the Reward Points earned by that
specific project to the CurseForge account with username antrakt92 using
CurseForge's project Members reward-allocation feature. Keep that allocation
in effect for as long as the project earns points and involves Meaningful
Reuse of the Covered Material. This is not 10% of the publisher's account
balance, other projects, donations or other revenue.

The minimum allocation to antrakt92 is 10% in total per earning project, not
10% per reused source project, feature or file. The same allocation satisfies
this condition for all Antrakt/Antrakt92 projects licensed under these terms;
using several such projects does not increase the minimum to 20%, 30% or more.

No separate permission request, private message or negotiated agreement is
required. Send the project member invitation required by CurseForge and set
the allocation when the platform permits it. An outstanding invitation awaiting
the author's acceptance does not by itself breach this condition; once accepted,
the allocation must be enabled before further reward accrual where the platform
permits. No payment is required for a project that does not earn these points.
Ordinary installation, gameplay, links and collections that merely reference
the original project do not trigger this condition.

